        "objective": "Create 100 TIER_1 grocery items for a React Native shopping list app (`shadowlist`). Write ONLY the array — no imports, no exports, no interface definitions.\n\nRules:\n- Each item has: `{ nameEn: string, nameDe: string, foodType: FoodType, icon: string, category: string, tier: 1 }`\n- Valid foodTypes: grain, dairy, meat, fish, fruit, vegetable, egg, sugar, beverage, oil, nuts, legumes, spice, non_food\n- Valid categories: Groceries, Beverages, Snacks, Household, Personal\n- Icon must be a valid MaterialCommunityIcons name (common ones like 'bread-slice-outline', 'fruit-cherries', 'carrot', 'cheese', 'rice', 'coffee', 'fish', 'egg-outline', 'food-drumstick-outline', 'bottle-wine', 'candy', 'cow', 'seed', etc.)\n- These should be the most common grocery items (top-100 frequency)\n- German names should be accurate grocery translations\n- Distribution: ~15% vegetables, ~12% fruit, ~10% grain, ~10% dairy, ~8% meat/fish/egg, ~10% beverages, ~8% sugar/snacks, ~7% condiments/oils/spices, ~5% household/non_food, ~15% other groceries\n\nWrite the raw TypeScript array, one item per line. Format:\n```typescript\n  { nameEn: 'Milk', nameDe: 'Milch', foodType: 'dairy', icon: 'cheese', category: 'Groceries', tier: 1 },\n  { nameEn: '...', nameDe: '...', foodType: '...', icon: '...', category: '...', tier: 1 },\n```\nEXACTLY 100 items. No header, no footer, no interface. Just the array entries.",
