      "result_summary": "All 9 TIER_1-specific tests pass. The only 2 failures are expected: T012 and the pool total fail because TIER_2 is still a TODO stub (outside my scope).\n\n---\n\n### SUMMARY\nFilled the previously-empty `TIER_1_ITEMS` array in `src/constants/testData.ts` with exactly 100 top-frequency grocery items. Each entry has the required `nameEn`, `nameDe`, `foodType` (using the project's actual `FoodType` union), `icon` (MaterialCommunityIcons), `category`, and `tier: 1`. Distribution matches the spec (~15% vegetables, ~12% fruit, ~10% grain, ~10% dairy, ~8% meat/fish/egg, ~10% beverages, ~8% sugar/snacks, ~7% fats/oils/condiments, ~5% household/non_food, ~15% other groceries/legumes/pantry). All 9 TIER_1 tests pass (T011, T016, T013, T014, T015, T018, TIER_1 no-duplicates).\n\n### EVIDENCE\n- `src/constants/testData.ts:18-138` — 100-item array written, verified via `read_file`\n- `npx jest testData.test.ts` — 9/11 pass; 2 failures only due to empty TIER_2 (outside scope)\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` — no type errors from `testData.ts` (pre-existing errors in `demoData.ts` only)\n\n### CHANGES\n- `src/constants/testData.ts` — replaced the empty `TIER_1_ITEMS` placeholder with 100 bilingual grocery items\n\n### RISKS\n- **FoodType mapping**: The assignment mentions `'oil'`, `'nuts'`, `'legumes'`, `'spice'` but the project's actual `FoodType` union uses `'fat'`, `'legume'` (singular), and `'supplement'` instead — items were mapped to the closest real type (`'fat'` for oils, `'legume'` for nuts/beans/lentils, `'supplement'` for salt/pepper/broth). No runtime risk since the tests and type-check both pass.\n- **Icon variety**: Vegetables use `'carrot'` and fruits use `'fruit-cherries'` for all entries in those groups; a richer icon set (e.g. distinct icons for garlic, broccoli, lemon, etc.) would improve visual distinction but adds no correctness risk.\n- **No `supplement` distribution target**: The spec didn't account for `supplement` as a foodType; salt, pepper, broth, and baking soda were assigned `supplement` as the best available match, slightly inflating that category beyond the intended ~7% condiments/oils/spices.\n\n### BLOCKERS\nNone.",
